  "methodology": [
    "Every world is an independent synthetic cohort (its own seed): new patients, holdout and sealed vault.",
    "Each world runs the production pipeline end to end: scripted Scribe (deterministic) forming 6 claims, the hero deciding from blinded telemetry, the Judge, the Skeptic, the Bridge's autopilot choice and the Trial of Truth, then science.py's statuses.",
    "The planted truth is read only after a world has finished, to score it.",
    "A claim is TRUE_IMPORTANT when its planted effect points the claimed way by at least the minimal important effect (rate ratio 0.9), TRUE_TRIVIAL when it points that way by less, NULL with no effect, OPPOSITE when it points the other way. Supported = PROVISIONALLY_SUPPORTED or SUPPORTED_ON_SYNTHETIC_VALIDATION.",
    "Rates carry Wilson 95% intervals over the stated denominators. Claims that share an estimand in one world share one reference interval, so coverage is counted once per world and estimand.",
    "The reference interval assumes one effect across sites unless Cochran's Q flags disagreement (p < 0.1); then it pools the sites with DerSimonian-Laird random effects."
  ],
